**Remediation:**

Use `jwt.verify()` with an explicit secret/key and algorithm restriction:

```typescript
import jwt from "jsonwebtoken";

const JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;
if (!JWT_SECRET) throw new Error("JWT_SECRET must be set");

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(" ")[1];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).send("No token");

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET, {
      algorithms: ["HS256"], // Explicit algorithm restriction
    });
    if (decoded && (decoded as any).role === "admin") {
      req.user = decoded;
      next();
    } else {
      res.status(403).send("Forbidden");
    }
  } catch (err) {
    res.status(401).send("Invalid token");
  }
});
```

Key changes:
- `jwt.decode()` → `jwt.verify()` with a secret
- Explicit `algorithms` array prevents algorithm confusion attacks (CWE-757)
- `try/catch` handles expired, malformed, or invalid tokens
- Secret sourced from environment variable

