Additionally, the read-modify-write cycle on lines 16–18 is not atomic — concurrent `/register` requests will race, and one write can overwrite another's data (lost update).

**Impact:** Disk I/O latency is unpredictable (microseconds on SSD, milliseconds on spinning disk or under load). Combined with PERF-001, a single `/register` request can block the event loop for 300ms+ (bcrypt) plus disk I/O time. The race condition means concurrent registrations will silently lose user records.

**Recommendation:**
```javascript
