### API-002: Missing Body Parser — `req.body` Will Be `undefined`

- **Rule ID**: API-002
- **Severity**: **critical**
- **Location**: Lines 3–14 — no `express.json()` middleware registered; `req.body.id` accessed on line 12
- **Description**: Express does not parse JSON request bodies by default. Without `app.use(express.json())`, `req.body` is `undefined`, so `req.body.id` on line 12 will throw a `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'id')`. This crashes the request handler and, without error-handling middleware, Express will send a default HTML 500 error containing a stack trace.
- **Evidence**: No call to `app.use(express.json())` or any body-parsing middleware anywhere in the provided code. Line 12 accesses `req.body.id`.
- **Recommendation**: Register body-parsing middleware before route definitions:

```typescript
