```

The default Java `DocumentBuilderFactory` configuration **enables** processing of external entities (DTDs, external general entities, external parameter entities). No calls to `factory.setFeature(...)` or `factory.setAttribute(...)` are made to restrict this.

**Exploit Scenario:**

An attacker supplies the following payload as `xmlInput`:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE foo [
  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///etc/passwd">
]>
<root>&xxe;</root>
```

This causes the parser to:
1. **Read arbitrary local files** (e.g., `/etc/passwd`, application config files with database credentials).
2. **Perform Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)** via `http://` or `https://` URIs in the entity definition, scanning internal networks.
3. **Cause Denial of Service** via recursive entity expansion ("Billion Laughs" attack).

**Remediation:**

Apply the OWASP-recommended defensive configuration before creating the `DocumentBuilder`:

```java
import javax.xml.XMLConstants;
import javax.xml.parsers.*;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.xml.sax.InputSource;
import java.io.*;

public class XmlProcessor {
    public Document parse(String xmlInput) throws Exception {
        DocumentBuilderFactory factory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();

        // Prevent XXE
        factory.setFeature(XMLConstants.FEATURE_SECURE_PROCESSING, true);
        factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
        factory.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
        factory.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
        factory.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd", false);
        factory.setXIncludeAware(false);
        factory.setExpandEntityReferences(false);

        DocumentBuilder builder = factory.newDocumentBuilder();
        return builder.parse(new InputSource(new StringReader(xmlInput)));
    }
}
```

The most critical single line is disabling DOCTYPE declarations entirely (`disallow-doctype-decl`), which blocks all DTD-based XXE vectors at the root.

